@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@
+# MDBList playback tracking
+
+This change adds outgoing movie and episode playback tracking to Nuvio Native
+Legacy 2.0.2. Existing MDBList rating queries, Trakt, Simkl and Nuvio progress
+remain independent. It does not import MDBList history, replace Continue
+watching, synchronize the library, or send manual watched/unwatched actions.
+
+## Enable it
+
+1. Add your personal MDBList API key in your Nuvio account's existing MDBList
+   credential settings and allow account sync to finish. A private
+   `art/mdblist.txt` file containing the key is also supported by the existing
+   loader. Do not distribute a build containing your key.
+2. Rebuild/install with the project's normal instructions for your platform.
+   The existing build scripts discover `src/*.c`, including the new modules.
+3. Open **Settings → Account and profiles → Tracking → Track playback with
+   MDBList** and turn it on. Portuguese labels are **Ajustes → Conta e perfis →
+   Rastreamento → Rastrear reprodução no MDBList**.
+4. Check **MDBList tracking status** on the same screen. `Ready to track` means a key is
+   available and there is no current delivery failure; it is not a live key
+   validation. The first playback request validates the credential with MDBList.
+
+Tracking is off by default and saved per profile on this device. A new profile,
+an older profile snapshot without this setting, and logout reset it to off.
+This consent is not written into the official web client's settings blob.
+The API key is the existing Nuvio account credential; each enabled profile using
+that key sends playback to the same MDBList account. Turning off the MDBList
+ratings switch does not turn off playback tracking.
+
+## Playback behavior
+
+- Start after the player's existing five seconds of continuous valid playback.
+- Pause on pause/buffering, resume with start, and refresh actual progress at
+  most once per minute during playback.
+- Stop on player exit/episode transition/suspension, using the actual player
+  position rather than the local credits/completion rounding.
+- MDBList marks watched on **stop at 80% or more**. Below 80%, stop saves paused
+  progress. Rounding a percentage just below 80% cannot cross that boundary.
+  The existing Trakt completion rules are unchanged.
+- Episodes identify the show and season/episode numbers. IMDb and the app's
+  typed `tmdb:m123` / `tmdb:t123:season:episode` IDs are supported, including
+  season zero. Bare shows, unresolved addon/anime identifiers, live channels,
+  personal-server items and error clips under two minutes are skipped.
+- A bounded, ordered background queue preserves an episode's stop before the
+  next episode's start. Playback/UI does not wait for HTTP.
+
+## Failure handling and limits
+
+Temporary transport and server failures get two retries, after 30 and 120
+seconds, while the app remains open. Other ordinary client errors are not
+retried. A rejected key (401/403) blocks further writes until reconfiguration;
+correct the account credential and allow sync to complete.
+
+For HTTP 429, queued work waits until the next UTC day. This is deliberately
+conservative: the app's existing network interface does not expose
+`Retry-After`, and MDBList has both daily and five-minute account quotas.
+The status row explains the wait. Ratings requests and other clients share
+the same account quota.
+
+The queue is memory-only, bounded at 32 pending events, and cancelled on
+profile/key changes, disabling tracking, or logout. A request already
+dispatched cannot be recalled. Closing/killing the app can lose pending
+events; disabling tracking leaves any previously started server session to
+expire. Nothing is presented as a confirmed local watched-history sync.
+Credentials, request URLs and API response bodies are not logged by the new
+tracker. The existing network layer logs only a sanitized host on errors.
+
+## Documentation verified on 8 October 2026
+
+- [Official MDBList API overview](https://docs.mdblist.com/docs/api)
+- [Official API explorer](https://api.mdblist.com/docs/)
+- [Official OpenAPI schema](https://api.mdblist.com/schema/)
+- [MDBList scrobbling reference](https://mdblist.docs.apiary.io/reference/external-lists/list-items)
+
+The current schema documents `POST /scrobble/start`, `/scrobble/pause` and
+`/scrobble/stop`, API-key query authentication and OAuth bearer authentication.
+The integration uses the already available personal API key. Its flat episode
+payload is `{"show":{"ids":{"tmdb":1396},"season":1,"episode":2},"progress":10}`.
+It does not reuse Trakt's separate top-level `episode` object.
+
+## Validation and remaining device checks
+
+Executed successfully in this workspace:
+
+- New deterministic C transport/payload tests (`tests/mdblist.sh` equivalent):
+  movie/episode JSON, IMDb/TMDB IDs, specials, invalid IDs, locale-safe numbers,
+  80% boundary, event deduplication, ordered episode transitions, minute refresh,
+  absent/rejected/malformed keys, consent/profile changes, stale in-flight
+  responses, retry timing, API quota delay, worker creation failure and queue
+  capacity. HTTP, threads and time are controlled test doubles.
+- Existing Trakt scrobble regression tests.
+- Existing runtime language regression tests and all 28 translation-table checks.
+- Existing settings catalog check (262 options, each represented once).
+- Compilation of every modified application C file to Linux/musl objects with
+  the actual SDL and Khronos headers. This checks source compatibility, not a
+  linked TV/Android release.
+
+New assertions were also added to the existing factory-default and profile
+settings suites. Those full suites require the project's SDL/graphics runtime
+and were not executed here. New strings have English entries and retain table
+alignment; other languages use English for these additions.
+
+No real MDBList account write, full target release build, installation or TV
+playback test was performed. Before using this as your regular build:
+
+1. Build for the intended TV/Android platform using the normal toolchain.
+2. Confirm that playback with tracking off produces no MDBList writes.
+3. Enable tracking; play an IMDb movie and a TMDB-backed episode. Confirm
+   start, pause/resume, progress and stop in MDBList.
+4. Stop below 80% to confirm saved progress, then stop at/above 80% to confirm
+   watched history. Test next-episode transition and a season-zero special.
+5. Switch profiles/logout and confirm tracking does not carry over without
+   that profile's opt-in. Verify the existing Trakt/Simkl behavior still works.
+
+Run the focused network-free tests on a normal development host with:
+
+```sh
+bash tests/mdblist.sh
+bash tests/trakt_scrobble.sh
+python3 tools/idiomas.py
+python3 tests/ajustes_secoes.py src/ajustes.c
+```
